[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mAllowlist for remote (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOnly explicitly permitted keys are serialized to the sink; unknown keys are dropped by default. Console still shows
[39m     [38;5;246mfull detail locally. Future careless log calls cannot leak, at the cost of registering each new remote field.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Denylist redaction
     [38;5;246mShip what is passed, masking keys matching password/token/secret/auth/cookie. Convenient, but only catches [39m
     [38;5;246manticipated patterns; a nested or oddly-named credential still gets through.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m No enforced policy
     [38;5;246mTransmit what is logged and rely on code review to keep secrets out. Least friction, highest chance of an eventual
[39m     [38;5;246mcredential leak from a page that handles passwords.[39m
